---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Home" description="A community-driven programme for hadron and QCD physics at GSI and FAIR.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid"></div><div class="orb orb-one"></div><div class="orb orb-two"></div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> AN INTERNATIONAL SCIENCE INITIATIVE</p>
      <h1>Exploring the<br /><em>strong interaction.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">A new era of hadron physics at GSI and FAIR — connecting precision experiments, advanced theory, and a global scientific community.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/science/">Explore the science <span>↗</span></a><a class="button button-ghost" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15986" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the White Paper <span>↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-graphic" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="graphic-ring ring-a"></div><div class="graphic-ring ring-b"></div><div class="graphic-ring ring-c"></div>
      <div class="nucleus"><span>QCD</span><small>MATTER</small></div>
      <i class="particle p1"></i><i class="particle p2"></i><i class="particle p3"></i><i class="particle p4"></i>
      <span class="graphic-label label-a">CONFINEMENT</span><span class="graphic-label label-b">HADRON STRUCTURE</span><span class="graphic-label label-c">DYNAMICS</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-foot"><span>GSI HELMHOLTZZENTRUM · FAIR</span><span>FROM SIS18 TO SIS100 AND BEYOND</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="intro section-wrap">
    <div class="section-kicker">THE BIG QUESTION <span>01 / 04</span></div>
    <div class="intro-grid"><h2>How does the<br /><em>strong force</em><br />build our world?</h2><div class="intro-copy"><p class="lead">Quantum Chromodynamics is the theory of the strong interaction — yet many of its most fascinating consequences emerge where calculations are hardest.</p><p>How do quarks and gluons form the rich spectrum of hadrons? What binds hadrons together? How does matter behave at high baryon density? QCD at FAIR brings together experimental and theoretical expertise to address these questions with intense hadron beams and versatile detector systems.</p><a class="text-link" href="/science/">Discover the research themes <span>→</span></a></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="framework-section section-wrap">
    <div class="section-kicker">THE QCDatFAIR FRAMEWORK <span>THE CENTRAL IDEA</span></div>
    <div class="framework-heading">
      <div><h2>One facility.<br /><em>Connected questions.</em></h2></div>
      <p>Hadron beams at GSI and FAIR provide the common foundation for a coordinated programme spanning the composition, interactions, production and dynamics of strongly interacting matter.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="framework-figure">
      <img src="/images/qcdatfair-framework.png" alt="QCDatFAIR framework: hadron beams at GSI and FAIR connect hadron structure and spectroscopy, few-body interactions, hadron production, heavy-ion dynamics, and reference measurements." loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>The QCDatFAIR framework: complementary research directions connected through hadron beams at GSI and FAIR.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="framework-pillars">
      <div><span>01</span><b>Composition of hadrons</b><small>Structure · Spectroscopy</small></div>
      <div><span>02</span><b>Interactions</b><small>Few-body · Hadron–hadron</small></div>
      <div><span>03</span><b>Production & dynamics</b><small>Hadron production · Heavy-ion dynamics</small></div>
      <div><span>04</span><b>Reference measurements</b><small>π/p + A · A + A</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="themes-band">
    <div class="section-wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-kicker">SCIENCE DRIVERS <span>02 / 04</span></div><h2>Four windows into<br /><em>non-perturbative QCD.</em></h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/science/">All research themes →</a></div>
      <div class="theme-grid">
        <a class="theme-card" href="/science/#interactions"><span class="card-index">01</span><div class="theme-symbol">↔</div><h3>Hadron interactions</h3><p>Scattering, bound states, and the forces between hadrons.</p><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="theme-card" href="/science/#spectroscopy"><span class="card-index">02</span><div class="theme-symbol">◉</div><h3>Hadron spectroscopy</h3><p>Mapping baryons, mesons, and the spectrum of exotic states.</p><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="theme-card" href="/science/#structure"><span class="card-index">03</span><div class="theme-symbol">⌁</div><h3>Hadron structure</h3><p>Electromagnetic form factors and transition dynamics.</p><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="theme-card" href="/science/#matter"><span class="card-index">04</span><div class="theme-symbol">✳</div><h3>QCD matter</h3><p>In-medium properties and connections to dense astrophysical matter.</p><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="roadmap section-wrap">
    <div class="section-kicker">A PHASED RESEARCH PROGRAMME <span>03 / 04</span></div><div class="section-heading"><h2>One vision.<br /><em>Multiple frontiers.</em></h2><p class="section-aside">A staged programme that builds on existing capabilities and expands with the evolving GSI/FAIR accelerator complex.</p></div>
    <div class="roadmap-line">
      <article class="phase"><span class="phase-dot"></span><span class="phase-tag">NOW · SIS18</span><h3>Build the foundations</h3><p>Precision hadron physics with existing facilities, including HADES and secondary pion beams.</p><span class="phase-code">01 — SIS18</span></article>
      <article class="phase"><span class="phase-dot"></span><span class="phase-tag">NEXT · SIS100</span><h3>Expand the reach</h3><p>High-intensity proton beams and high-rate experiments, with CBM as a key facility.</p><span class="phase-code">02 — SIS100</span></article>
      <article class="phase"><span class="phase-dot"></span><span class="phase-tag">HORIZON · HESR</span><h3>Precision with antiprotons</h3><p>Explore the hadron landscape with the stored antiproton programme and PANDA.</p><span class="phase-code">03 — HESR</span></article>
    </div>
    <p class="note">The roadmap is indicative; implementation and schedules depend on facility readiness and programme decisions.</p>
  </section>


  <section class="paper-cta">
    <div class="paper-art" aria-hidden="true"><div class="paper-orbit"></div><div class="paper-core">QCD<span>at FAIR</span></div><span class="paper-coord">arXiv:2512.15986</span></div>
    <div class="paper-copy"><div class="section-kicker">THE COMMUNITY WHITE PAPER <span>04 / 04</span></div><h2>Hadron Physics<br /><em>Opportunities at FAIR.</em></h2><p>A community-wide vision for a decade-spanning programme of hadron and QCD studies, connecting intense deuteron, proton and pion beams with high-rate detectors and an international theory effort.</p><a class="button button-light" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.15986" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read on arXiv <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
